hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"439","Anyone who is pleased that his sustenance is expanded and his age extended should do kindness to his near relatives. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1693)"
"440","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, the virtue for which the reward is received most quickly is maintaining the ties of kinship. Indeed, there are families whose people are sinners, but their wealth increases and their numbers grow when they maintain the ties of kinship. And there is no family whose people maintain the ties of kinship with one another except that they will not be in need."
"441","Verily Allah created the universe and when He had finished that, ties of relationship came forward and said This is the place for him who seeks refuge from severing (of blood-relationship). He said: Yes. Are you not satisfied that I should keep relationship with one who joins your ties of relationship and sever it with one who severs your (ties of relationship)? They (the ties of blood) said: Certainly so. Thereupon He said: Well, that is how things are for you. Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: Recite if you like:"" But if you turn away you are sure to make mischief in the land and cut off the ties of kinship. Those it is whom Allah has cursed, so He has made them deaf and blinded their eyes. Do they not reflect on the Qur'an? Or, are there locks on their hearts?"". (Using translation from Muslim 2554)"
"442","I have been cut off. I have been wronged. So its Lord says to it: Are you not pleased that I will cut off the one who cuts you off, and I will join the one who joins you?"
"443","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah the Exalted has said: I am Compassionate, and this has been derived from mercy. I have derived its name from My name. If anyone joins it, I shall join him, and if anyone cuts it off, I shall cut him off. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1694)"
"444","I was wronged. I was treated badly. I was severed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then its Lord will reply: Are you not pleased that I will cut off the one who severed you, and I will join the one who maintained you?”"
"445","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The womb (ties of kinship) is hanging from the Throne, and the one who does good in return for good is not considered as maintaining the ties of kinship. The one who truly maintains the ties of kinship is the person who, when his ties of kinship are severed, still maintains them."
"446","the Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever has three daughters, or three sisters, or two daughters, or two sisters and he keeps good company with them and fears Allah regarding them, then Paradise is for him. (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1916)"
"447","I and that person will be in Paradise like this.” The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) indicated this by joining his middle finger and the finger next to it. These words of the narration are as transmitted by Ibrahim bin Hasan ‘Allaf. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): “I and he will be in Paradise like these two,” refers to entering and preceding (in Paradise). It does not mean that the person who takes care of two daughters or two sisters will attain the same rank in Paradise as the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"448","A poor woman came to me along with her daughters. I gave her three dates. She gave a date to each of them and then she took up one date and brought that to her mouth in order to eat that, but her daughters expressed desire to eat it. She then divided the date that she intended to eat between them. This (kind) treatment of her impressed me and I mentioned that which she did to Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Thereupon he said: Verily Allah has assured Paradise for her, because of (this act) of her, or He has rescued her from Hell-Fire. (Using translation from Muslim 2630)"
"449","I should not look towards someone above me, but rather look towards someone below me. He advised me to love the poor and to stay close to them. He advised me to maintain ties of kinship even if they turn away from me. He advised me not to fear the blame of any blamer regarding Allah. He advised me to speak the truth even if it is bitter. And he advised me to frequently recite ""La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah,"" for it is one of the treasures of Paradise."
"450","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the situation is as you describe, then you are throwing ashes upon them. As long as you continue doing so, Allah Almighty's help will remain with you."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The word ""al-mil"" used in the text of the narration refers to such ashes in which there are pieces of embers (i.e., burning coals)."
"451","Messenger of Allah, I have relatives with whom I try, to have close relationship, but they sever (this relation). I treat them well, but they treat me ill. I am sweet to them but they are harsh towards me. Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said: If it is so as you say, then you in fact throw hot ashes (upon their faces) and there would always remain with you on behalf of Allah (an Angel to support you) who would keep you dominant over them so long as you adhere to this (path of righteousness). (Using translation from Muslim 2558a)"
"452","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyida Asma (may Allah be pleased with her): Yes! Maintain ties of kinship with her."
"453","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Yes."
"454","The Prophet ﷺ said: Anyone who cuts off relationship from his nearest relatives will not enter Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1696)"
"455","The Prophet ﷺ said: There is no sin more fitted to have punishment meted out by Allah to its perpetrator in advance in this world along with what He stores up for him in the next world than oppression and severing ties of relationship. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4902)"
"456","The Prophet ﷺ said: There is no sin more fitted to have punishment meted out by Allah to its perpetrator in advance in this world along with what He stores up for him in the next world than oppression and severing ties of relationship. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4902)"
"457","I have ten children and I have never kissed any of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who does not show tenderness will not be shown tenderness. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5218)"
"458","narrates as a marfu’ hadith to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): He (peace be upon him) said: “He has no connection with us who does not respect elders, does not show mercy to the young, does not enjoin good, and does not forbid evil.”"
"459","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to go to meet the Ansar. He would greet their children with salam and would place his hand on their heads."
"460","the Messenger of Allah said: "" I and the sponsor of an orphan shall be in Paradise like these two.""And he indicaed with his fingers, meaning his index and his middle finger (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1918)"
"461","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Go to her and tell her that whatever Allah takes back belongs to Him, and whatever He gives also belongs to Him, and everything has a fixed term in His presence. Therefore, she should be patient and hope for reward. The narrator says: After a while, that person returned and said: O Messenger of Allah! She is insisting by oath that you must come to her. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) stood up, and we also stood up with him. Some of the Ansar were with us. We went to her, and the child was presented to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and his breath was rattling in his chest. Tears flowed from the eyes of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah! What is this? The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""This is mercy, which Allah has placed in the hearts of His servants, and Allah only shows mercy to those of His servants who are merciful."
"462","I heard Sayyiduna Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who is truthful and believed, saying: ""Mercy is only separated from the wretched."
"463","I have ten children and I have never kissed any of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who does not show tenderness will not be shown tenderness. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5218)"
"464","narrates this as a marfu’ hadith to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: “He is not one of us who does not respect the elder, does not show mercy to the younger, does not enjoin good, and does not forbid evil.”"
"465",""" That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who shows no mercy to the people, Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, does not show mercy to him."" (Using translation from Muslim 2319a)"
"466","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Mercy is only separated from the wretched."
"467","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah does not show mercy to him."
"468","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not consider any good deed insignificant. If you have nothing to give, then deal with people gently and meet them with a cheerful face."
"469","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Every gentle, approachable, and easy-going person has been made forbidden for Hell."
"470","The people said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every easy-going, gentle, approachable, and lenient person."
"471","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dealing with people with good manners is charity."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The kind treatment that is considered charity for the one who practices it means: a person should make praiseworthy things a part of his character. Along with this, he should keep away from anything in which there is a possibility of disobeying Allah Almighty. Whereas, by indulgence (mudahanat) is meant that a person adopts those traits which are considered good in dealings with people, and among them is included something that Allah Almighty does not like."
"472","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Speaking a good word is charity, and every step taken towards the mosque is charity."
"473","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Save yourselves from the Fire, even if it is by giving half a date (in charity), and if you do not find that, then (save yourselves) through a good word.”"
"474","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your smiling at your brother is also charity."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Zumail is Simak bin Waleed Hanafi Yamani, and he is trustworthy, while the narrator named Nasr bin Muhammad is Jurashi Yamani, and Nadr bin Muhammad is Quraishi Marwazi, who was a man of opinion, and both of them lived in the same era."
"475","I related this to Abu'l-‘Aliyah, and he said: We have also heard it in this way. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The words of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), ""They brought a qina‘ juz’ to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him),"" refer to a tray of dates, because the people of Madinah use the word ""qina‘"" for a tray, and the word ""juz’"" for dates."
"476","“The Prophet ﷺ was asked: ‘What most admits people to Paradise?’ He said: ‘Piety and good manners.’ And he was asked: ‘What most leads people to Hell?’ He said: ‘The two hollow ones: The mouth and the private part.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4246)"
"477","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not use obscene language. He did not display foul speech. He used to say: ""The best among you are those who have the best character."
"478","The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Of the things given to a Muslim servant, which is the best?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good character."
"479","The Prophet ﷺ said: The most perfect believer in respect of faith is he who is best of them in manners. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4682)"
"480","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: By his good character a believer will attain the degree of one who prays during the night and fasts during the day. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4798)"
"481","The heaviest thing in the scale is good character.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named ‘Ata is ‘Ata bin Abdullah, and Kaikharan is the name of a place in Yemen. Sayyida Umm Darda’ the younger was named Hujaymah bint Hayyi, while the elder Sayyida Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) was named Khayrah bint Abu Hudard Ansariyyah, and she was a female companion."
"482","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Indeed, the most beloved of you to Allah Almighty and the closest of you to me are those who have the best character among you. And the most disliked of you to Allah Almighty and the farthest of you from me are those who talk excessively, exaggerate in their speech, and speak in an affected manner.”"
"483","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A man's honor is his religion. His dignity is his intellect, and his lineage is his character."
"484","The people said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah! The Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Those whose lives are the longest and whose character is the best."
"485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those among you who have the best character."
"486","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O people! Allah Almighty has removed hardship from you. Except for the person who tries to dishonor his brother. This is the person who will commit sin and will be destroyed. The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! Can we use medicine? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes! Allah Almighty has sent down a cure for every disease that He has sent down. There is only one disease that is different. The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! Which one is that? He said: Old age. The people asked: Who is the most beloved person to Allah Almighty? O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The most beloved among the people to Allah Almighty is the one who has the best character."
"487","""On the Day of Uhud, sixty-four of the Ansar were killed, and six from the Muhajirin, one of whom was Hamzah, and they mutilated them, so the Ansar said: 'If, (in the future) we are able to kill them on a day like this, we would mutilate from among them as twice as they (mutilate from among us).'"" He said: ""So on the day of the Conquest of Makkah, Allah revealed: And if you punish them, then punish them with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you have patience, then it is better for those who are patient (16:126). So a man said: 'There shall be no Quraish after today.' But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave the people, except for four.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3129)"
"488","I never saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) hitting any servant. Nor did he ever hit any of his wives, nor did he ever strike anything with his hand, except during jihad in the way of Allah (when he would strike the enemies). And whenever anyone wronged him, he never took revenge for himself; but if it was for the sake of Allah Almighty (he would take revenge), because if any matter was for Allah Almighty, then he would take revenge for it. And whenever two situations were presented before him, he would choose the one that was easier, provided it was not sinful, because if it was sinful, then he would be the farthest from it."
"489","""Worship the Most Merciful and spread (the greeting of) peace.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3694)"
"490","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said, ""You must speak good words and spread the greeting of peace."
"491","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Spread the greeting of peace, you will remain safe.”"
"492","that he asked Anas bin Malik: ""Did the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ use to shake each other's hand?"" He said, ""Yes."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2729)"
"493","The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: He received ten good deeds. Then another man passed by and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Twenty good deeds. Then another man passed by and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Thirty good deeds. Then one of those present stood up and did not offer greetings, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: It is possible that your companion did not forget (to greet). Whoever comes to a gathering should offer greetings; if he wishes, he may sit there, and if he wishes to leave, he should offer greetings again, because the first is not more entitled than the second."
"494","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When one of you arrives at the gathering, then give the Salam, and if he is given a place to sit, then let him sit. Then when he stands, let him give the Salam, the first is more worthy than the last."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2706)"
"495","The Prophet ﷺ said: When one of you comes to an assembly, he should give a salutation and if he feels inclined to get up, he should give a salutation, for the former is not more of a duty than the latter. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5208)"
"496","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When one of you arrives at the gathering, then give the Salam, and if he is given a place to sit, then let him sit. Then when he stands, let him give the Salam, the first is more worthy than the last."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2706)"
"497","The rider should greet the one who is walking, and the one who is walking should greet the one who is sitting, and the smaller group should greet the larger group."
"498","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A rider should greet the one who is walking, the one who is walking should greet the one who is sitting, and among two people walking, the one who greets first will have greater virtue."
"499","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""There are three people whose guarantee is upon Allah Almighty: if they remain alive, they will be provided sustenance and their needs will be fulfilled, and if they die, Allah Almighty will admit them into Paradise. Whoever enters his house and greets (with Salam), that person is under the guarantee of Allah Almighty; and whoever goes out towards the mosque, he is under the guarantee of Allah Almighty; and whoever goes out in the path of Allah (for jihad), he is under the guarantee of Allah Almighty."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: Muhammad bin Mu’afi did not eat anything from the pure things of the world for eighteen years; at the time of breaking the fast, he used to drink broth, etc."
"500","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""Do not initiate the greeting of peace to the People of the Book. When you meet them on the road, force them to take the narrower path.\"""""
"501","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not initiate greeting (salaam) to the People of the Book. When you see them on"
"502","When the Jews offer you salutations, some of them say as-Sam-u-'Alaikum (death be upon you). You should say (in response to it): Let it be upon you. (Using translation from Muslim 2164a)"
"503","The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: ""Do you know what he said?"" The people replied: ""Yes! He greeted us with Salam."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No. He said 'As-Saam Alaikum,' meaning your religion is weak."" So when any person from the People of the Book greets you (in this way), then you should say, 'Wa Alaik' (and the same be upon you), and the same be upon you."
"504","I decide between them. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: This is a good thing. And these children—Shurayh, Abdullah, and Muslim—the Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: Who is the eldest among them? He replied: Shurayh. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You are Abu Shurayh. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) called him and his children. When the people of his tribe were about to return to their area, the Prophet (peace be upon him) granted each person the land he liked in his area. So Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something that will make Paradise obligatory for me. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Speak good words, spread peace (salam), and feed others."
"505","A man asked the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him): When aspect of Islam is best? He replied: that you should provide food and greet both those you know and those you do not know. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5194)"
"506","He who believes in Allah and in the last day should honour his guest; he who believes in Allah and in the last day should not harm his neighbor; he who believes in Allah and in the last day should speak good or keep silence. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5154)"
"507","""Worship the Most Merciful and spread (the greeting of) peace.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3694)"
"508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread peace, feed (others), maintain ties of kinship, and pray at night when people are sleeping; you will enter Paradise in peace."
"509","The narrator named Ibn Mu'aniq is Abdullah bin Mu'aniq Ash'ari."
"510","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is one from whom people are safe, and a Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand (other) Muslims remain safe, and a migrant is the person who distances himself from evil. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, such a servant will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his harm."
"511","""Jibra'il kept enjoining good treatment of neighbours until I thought he would make neighbours heirs."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3674)"
"512","The Prophet ﷺ said ""Gabriel continued to recommend me about treating the neighbors Kindly and politely so much so that I thought he would order me to make them as my heirs. (Using translation from Bukhārī 6014)"
"513","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you cook a pot of food, add more broth to it, for it will be more accommodating for your family and your neighbors."
"514","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When you make broth, add more water to it, and then look at your neighbor's house and give them a suitable portion from it."
"515","I heard Layth narrating this. This is the first and last narration we have from Imam Malik on this authority. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says: Layth's statement that this is the first and last narration we have from Imam Malik on this authority is evidence that the narration which Qirad narrated from Layth, from Imam Malik, from Zuhri, from Urwah, and from Sayyidah Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, in which there is mention of the share of slaves, is a fabricated narration, which has no basis.)"
"516","He who believes in Allah and in the last day should honour his guest; he who believes in Allah and in the last day should not harm his neighbor; he who believes in Allah and in the last day should speak good or keep silence. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5154)"
"517","I said to Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him): Some of our neighbors drink alcohol. I want to call the officer so that he may arrest them. Sayyiduna Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Woe to you, do not do this, rather give them clear advice, warn them. He said: I have forbidden them, but they do not refrain. Now I will call the officer so that he may arrest them. Sayyiduna Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Woe to you, do not do this. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever conceals the faults of a believer, it is as if he saves a girl buried alive from her grave."
"518","""The companion who is the best to Allah is the one who is best to his companion. And the neighbor that is the best to Allah is the one that is best to his neighbor."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1944)"
"519","""The companion who is the best to Allah is the one who is best to his companion. And the neighbor that is the best to Allah is the one that is best to his neighbor."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1944)"
"520","I will never harm you again."
"521","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Fear Allah Almighty and do not consider any good deed insignificant (even if that good deed is) that you pour water from your bucket into the vessel of one who asks for water, or that you meet your brother with a cheerful face. And avoid letting your lower garment hang down, for this is among the signs of arrogance, and Allah Almighty does not like it. And if someone taunts you about a fault which he knows exists in you, then do not taunt him about something which you know exists in him. Let him do what he does; its burden will be upon him, and you will receive your reward. And never speak ill of anyone. The narrator says: After that, I never spoke ill of any animal or human being. Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""It is obligatory upon you to fear Allah Almighty,"" is a command that is obligatory upon all addressed people, that they should fear Allah Almighty in all circumstances. Whereas pouring water from your bucket into the bucket of one who asks for water, or meeting your Muslim brother with a cheerful face while talking to him, are actions whose command is for recommendation, and the purpose is to attain reward."
"522","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Never consider any good deed insignificant, even if that good deed is that you pour water from your bucket into the vessel of one who asks for water. Or that good deed is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face. And avoid letting your lower garment hang down, for this is a sign of arrogance, and Allah does not like it. And if someone says something bad to you regarding a fault which he knows is in you, then do not say something bad to him regarding a fault which you know is in him. Your reward will be given to you, and the burden will be upon the one who said that thing. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The command to not consider any good deed insignificant is such an instruction through which guidance is intended, and the prohibition of letting the lower garment hang down is a binding command due to a specific reason, and that is arrogance. So, when the reason of arrogance is absent, then there is no harm in letting the lower garment hang down. And when a person is spoken ill of, then the prohibition of speaking ill in return applies to that time, to before that time, and to after that time, even if the person was not spoken ill of."
"523","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not consider any good deed insignificant, even if it is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face. And when you make broth, add more water to it and send some of it to your neighbors."
"524","that Muʿādh b. Jabal planned to go on a journey, so he said: O Prophet of Allah, ˹please˺ give me some advice. He said, ""Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him."" He said: O Prophet of Allah, ˹please give me more advice.˺ He said, ""When you have done something bad, then ˹follow it up with˺ doing good."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, ˹please give me more advice.˺. He said, ""Be steadfast ˹in these˺ and improve your character."""
"525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When your neighbor says that you are good, then you are good; and when people say that you are bad, then you are bad."
"526","“A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ‘How can I know when I have done well and when I have done something bad?’ The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘If you hear your neighbors saying that you have done well, then you have done well, and if you hear them saying that you have done something bad, then you have done something bad.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4223)"
"527","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The best among you are those from whom good is expected and from whose evil people are safe, and your bad people are those from whom good is not expected and from whose evil people are not safe.”"
"528","'Shall I not inform you of the best of you from your worst?'"" He said: ""They became silent, so he said that three times, then a man said: 'Of course, O Messenger of Allah! Inform us of the best among us from our worst.' He said: 'The best of you is the one whose goodness is hoped for, and people are safe from his evil. And the worst of you is he whose goodness is not hoped for, and people are not safe from his evil.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2263)"
"529","""Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity, commanding good and forbidding evil is charity, your giving directions to a man lost in the land is charity for you. Your seeing for a man with bad sight is a charity for you, your removal of a rock, a thorn or a bone from the road is charity for you. Your pouring what remains from your bucket into the bucket of your brother is charity for you."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1956)"
"530","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever becomes a means of bringing good to his Muslim brother or easing his hardship before a ruler, Allah Almighty will make him cross the Bridge of Sirat on the Day of Judgment, on the day when feet will stumble."" These are the words of the narration as transmitted by Ibn Qutaybah. This was stated by the Sheikh."
"531","I have been given (wealth and property), so people ask from me and seek their needs from me, and you people are with me. You should intercede, you will be rewarded for it. Allah Almighty, through the tongue of His Prophet, decides whatever He likes and whatever He wills."" The Sheikh says: The narrator named Ibn Abu Burdah mentioned in this narration refers to the son of Ibn Abu Burdah. Imam Abu Hatim says: He is Buraid bin Abdullah bin Abu Burdah bin Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"532","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Whoever among you can benefit his brother, he should do so."
"533","A Muslim is a Muslim’s brother: he does not wrong him or abandon him. If anyone cares for his brother’s need, Allah will care for his need ; if anyone removes a Muslim’s anxiety, Allah will remove from him, on account of it, one of the anxieties of the Day of resurrection ; and if anyone conceals a Muslim’s fault, Allah will conceal his fault on the Day of resurrection. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4893)"
"534","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever conceals the faults of his Muslim brother, Allah Almighty will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter. And whoever relieves a Muslim of a difficulty, Allah Almighty will relieve him of the difficulties of the Day of Judgment. And Allah Almighty remains engaged in helping the servant as long as the servant is engaged in helping his brother."
"535","I am saying? He would reply: No. So regarding this, the verse was revealed: ""He frowned and turned away."
"536","While a person was going along the path he found a thorny branch upon it. He pushed it to a side and Allah approved (this action) of his and (as a mark of appreciation) granted him pardon. (Using translation from Muslim 1914b)"
"537","While a person was going along the path he found a thorny branch upon it. He pushed it to a side and Allah approved (this action) of his and (as a mark of appreciation) granted him pardon. (Using translation from Muslim 1914b)"
"538","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A man from among the people before you was brought to account, and in his record of deeds no good was found except for a thorny branch. That branch was lying on a path and was causing harm to people, so the man removed it from the way. Because of this, he was forgiven.”"
"539","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""All the past and future sins of a person were forgiven who had removed a thorny branch from the path of people (and set it aside)."
"540","The Prophet ﷺ said: A man never did a good deed but removed a thorny branch from the road; it was either in the tree and someone cut it and threw it on the road, or it was lying in it, he removed it. Allah accepted this good deed of his and brought him into Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5245)"
"541","""O Messenger of Allah! Tell me of an action by which I may benefit.' He said: 'Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3681)"
"542","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Give it water to drink, for there is a reward in doing good to every living being.”"
"543","The man felt compassion for it. He took off one of his socks, filled it with water, and gave the dog to drink. Allah Almighty accepted this deed of his and admitted him into Paradise."
"544","Abu Hurairah reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “ While a man was going on his way, he felt himself thirsty severely. He found a well and e went down in it. He drank water and came out. Suddenly he saw a dog panting and eating soil due to thirst. The man said (to himself) “This dog must have reached the same condition due to thirst as I had reached. So he went down into the well, filled his sock with water, held it with his mouth and came up. He supplied water to the dog. Allaah appreciated this and forgave him.” They asked “Apostle of Allaah ﷺ, Is there any reward for us for these beasts? He replied, For every cool liver there is a reward.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2550)"
"545","I was commanded to write.” Uyainah accepted it and tied it in his turban, but Aqra’ said, “Should I take a document about which I do not even know what is written in it? This would be like a document of deception.” Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) informed the Prophet (peace be upon him) about what both of them had said. The Prophet (peace be upon him) came out for some of his work, and he passed by a camel that was tied near the door of the mosque. This was in the early part of the day. When he passed by in the latter part of the day, the camel was still in the same condition. The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired, “Where is the owner of this camel?” He was searched for, but not found. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, “Fear Allah regarding these animals. Ride them when they are healthy, and eat them when they are fat.” Then the Prophet (peace be upon him), expressing displeasure, said, “Whoever asks for something while he already possesses that which makes him independent, he is only increasing the coals of Hell for himself.” That person asked, “O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by that which makes him independent?” The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, “His food for the morning and evening.” Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), “His food for the morning and evening,” means: he should always do so. “Ride them when they are healthy,” is evidence that regarding a sick and weak she-camel, it is necessary to refrain from riding her until she becomes healthy. And the statement of the Prophet (peace be upon him), “Eat them when they are fat,” is evidence that regarding a weak she-camel that has no marrow, it is preferable not to sacrifice her until she becomes fat and healthy."
"546","The same narration is also transmitted with another chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"547","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves gentleness in every matter."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Imam Malik has narrated only this narration from Imam Awza'i, whereas Awza'i has narrated four narrations from Imam Malik."
"548","He who is deprived of tenderly feelings is in fact deprived of good. (Using translation from Muslim 2592a)"
"549","""Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and He grants reward for it that He does not grant for harshness."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3688)"
"550","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came to this high (or low) ground and said to me: O Aisha! Be gentle with me, for gentleness beautifies whatever it is in, and when it is removed from something, it disgraces it."
"551","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Gentleness, wherever it is found, adorns it; and obscenity (that is, harshness), wherever it is found, spoils it."
"552","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿAllah is Kind and loves kindness, and He rewards for kindness in a way that He does not reward for harshness.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 902)"
